  "solution": "Logic:** 2 ×** **(First Number + Third Number) = Second Number**\n\nGiven:\n\n(14, 60, 16) \n\n→ 2 × (14 + 16)\n\n⇒ 2 × 30 = 60.\n\n(25, 80, 15) \n\n→ 2 × (25 + 15) \n\n⇒ 2 × 40 = 80.\n\nLet's check all the options as\n\n1) (21, 120, 15) \n\n→ 2 × (21 + 15) \n\n⇒ 2 × 36 = 72 ne 120\n\n2) (20, 30, 40) \n\n→ 2 × (20 + 40) \n\n⇒ 2 × 60 = 120 ne 30\n\n**3) (19, 80, 21) **\n\n**→ 2 × (19 + 21) **\n\n**⇒ 2 × 40 = 80**\n\n4) (15, 45, 30) \n\n→ 2 × (15 + 30) \n\n⇒ 2 × 45 = 90 ne 45\n\nThus, the set of numbers **(19, 80, 21)** follows the same pattern.\n\nHence, the correct answer is '__**option 3**__'.",
